  "HWS_SELECTED": "In world w* = ({W}, {q}, {sigma}, {p}) on a 12-high cylinder, under its documented law, on 32,768 fresh oracle-only histories: the phase-only oracle comparator D4 (the ideal belief-phase coordinate's covariance with r4 = m32 - m4, in the units of the K4b measure) has a one-sided lower bound {L3_D4} >= 0.03, 3x the K4b margin; the context gain G_C has lower bound {L3_GC} >= 0.10 nats; the beyond-four predictive gain G4 has lower bound {L3_G4} >= g4* = {g4_star}, and its circular-symbol part G4^A has lower bound {L3_G4A} >= g4A* = {g4A_star}. These are nominal bounds at alpha = 0.05/16. The world is the first qualifier in the frozen order (confidence class, then minimal departure). It does not license: (1) that any model learns it, captures any share of D4 or passes a learning gate; (2) that stage C will reach SUPPORT; (3) that D4 bounds a model's coordinate; (4) anything about the E4 models or any earlier verdict; (5) that w* is optimal, unique or the world where history matters most; (6) anything outside the grid.",
